{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789826824,"nonce":"XXL4HkiNsFG10+rdRTgkBhmfT80=","title":"SSA: a return nested in an if inside a block expression is dropped","message":"process_statement builds if/while blocks on demand for statements nested in a TypedExpression::Block (closure bodies, block-expression initializers), but has no Return arm: a return under such an if falls to the no-op default and the branch continues to the merge block. The CFG-builder path handles returns as terminators only.\n\nIts tail also returned the continuation block without taking it, so the next nested return, which does continuation_block.take().unwrap_or(block), put its terminator on the block the previous statement had already given a CondBranch: the condition is computed, then return; the then-block is unreachable.\n\nReproducer: a Lua chunk with a nested table constructor once every fallible call is followed by an inline check, local v = t.x.y prints the placeholder value and keeps going; local nested = { a = { b = {} } } exits the chunk at once. Pre-opt HIR shows the then-block as a bare br to the continuation, or a block ending in return right after a brcond condition.","files":null}]}